{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>A bright spot or a scab, etc.</b> They are names of afflictions — and some are whiter than others." "<b>Bright spot.</b> חֲבַרְבּוּרוֹת, טיי״א בְּלַעַז, and so ״בָּהִיר״ means bright in ״בַּשְּׁחָקִים״ (Job 37)." "<b>To Aaron, etc.</b> It is a decree of Scripture that the uncleanness of afflictions and their cleanness are only by the declaration of a priest (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {1 "the la'az טיי״א is Old French teile/taie, a term for a skin eruption or patch"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:04.345519124Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}